# Currency rules, Spanish. Same format as the French file (see there and docs/recognizers.md).
#
# [currency.symbol]: form | ISO 4217 code | prefix, suffix or both | confidence (optional).
# [currency.name]:   forms, comma-separated | ISO 4217 code | value of one in the currency (optional) | confidence (optional).
# A bare "peso" is the Mexican peso, the first of the many pesos; a named one (peso argentino) is the one named.

[currency.symbol]
$ | USD | both | 0.9
US$ | USD | prefix
MX$ | MXN | prefix
COP$ | COP | prefix
A$ | AUD | prefix
C$ | CAD | prefix
CA$ | CAD | prefix
€ | EUR | both
£ | GBP | both
¥ | JPY | both | 0.7
￥ | JPY | both | 0.7
₹ | INR | both
₩ | KRW | both
₽ | RUB | both
₺ | TRY | both
₪ | ILS | both
R$ | BRL | prefix

